---
title: Task status workflow — a blocked task always records a reason
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "To do" as pending
  state "In progress" as in_progress
  state "Blocked" as blocked
  state "Done" as completed
  state "Cancelled" as cancelled

  [*] --> pending: Advisor plans the task
  pending --> in_progress: Start
  pending --> blocked: Blocked ✱
  in_progress --> blocked: Blocked ✱
  blocked --> in_progress: Resume
  in_progress --> completed: Mark done
  completed --> in_progress: Reopen * (advisor)
  pending --> cancelled: Cancel * (advisor)
  in_progress --> cancelled: Cancel * (advisor)
  blocked --> cancelled: Cancel * (advisor)
  completed --> [*]
  cancelled --> [*]

  note right of blocked
    ✱ Reason enforced three times:
    1. update_task_status() refuses a blank reason
    2. CHECK on job_tasks: blocked ⇒ blocked_reason
    3. CHECK on job_task_history: blocked ⇒ reason
    The advisor and owners are notified with the reason.
  end note
  note left of in_progress
    The first task started moves an Approved job
    to In progress (system action "Work started").
    Job on hold: nothing can start, resume or reopen.
    Job cancelled: open tasks are cancelled with it.
    * = a reason is required
  end note
